8b48#` from `unknown.data` remains unverified.\n\n### Blocked\n- Initial scan job `j000002` failed with:\n  `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '$OUT/hits.json'`\n  It produced zero files and cannot support search conclusions.\n- A `job_run` using `profile=\"memory\"` was rejected:\n  `this run declared no job images: leave profile out (every job runs in dfirswarm-memory:symbols-arm64)`\n  Retried successfully without profile.\n- No exact Q14 userkey has yet been established.\n\n## Ledger\n- `limitation`, seq **2**: first targeted keyword scan `j000002` failed at output-write because `'$OUT/hits.json'` was literal; no result can be inferred. Recorded sensitive because the failed job used `secret_output`.\n- Unrecorded: successful findings from `j000014`, `j000024`, `j000030`, and pending `j000034`.\n\n## Board & Peers\n- `s42120100` **Contact provenance**: Q1/Q2; has Thunderbird dumpfiles work. Asked to share Q14-relevant profile/mail/database artifacts.\n- `s42120101` **Wallet trail**: Q5/Q10/Q11.\n- `s42120102` **Wallet trace**: Q5/Q9.\n- `s42120103` **Wallet history**: Q5/Q10/Q11; generated large Notepad dump `j000018`.\n- `s42120105`: Q12/Q13 database work bordering Q14. Asked for DBX filename/format/decryption/userkey context.\n- `s42120106` **Vault Artifact Analyst**: KeePass-focused output including `bruce.kdbx`; asked whether exact key was found.\n- `s42120107` **Memory triage**: process/files discovery.\n- `s42120108` briefly opened a duplicate DBX-key route for Q6, then closed it after only inspecting `unknown.data` header; reported it opaque and not probative.\n- `s42120109`: other memory work; no direct Q14 response captured.\n- No holds or vetoes observed.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Treat Q14 as potentially broader than literal `.dbx`**: Evidence shows `bruce.kdbx`, KeePass running, Thunderbird artifacts, and generic DBX hits; exact intended object remains unresolved.\n- **Do not promote `ry8bzv5c632r8b48#` yet**: It is a clear string