v6:m3`; use `j000067`/`j000130` instead.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] L-3/Q14 remains unresolved; the exact userkey has not been cryptographically established.\n- [ ] Need identify the actual historical Dropbox hostkeys/DBX encryption and key-derivation algorithm.\n- [ ] Need test the deleted KeePass password directly through the correct hostkeys and DBX codec, obtaining authentication or valid SQLite structure.\n- [ ] Jobs `j000131`, `j000144`, `j000148`, `j000149`, and `j000150` require ledger interpretation before the lead can end.\n\n### Blocked\n- No exact DBX format/decryptor has been located offline.\n- Initial `j000002` failed:\n  `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '$OUT/hits.json'`\n- `j000063` partially failed due `Unsupported Method` for RAR `v6:m3`.\n- `unrar` unavailable:\n  `/bin/bash: line 1: unrar: command not found`\n\n## Ledger\n- `limitation`, seq **2**: `j000002` failed because Python wrote to literal `$OUT/hits.json`.\n- `finding`, seq **31**: `j000030` inventory identifies `bruce.kdbx` and Thunderbird artifacts but no named standalone DBX.\n- `limitation`, seq **32**: `j000014`, `j000024`, and `j000034` broad searches did not identify Q14’s userkey.\n- `limitation`, seq **56**: `j000063` could not decode compressed RAR `v6:m3`; successful extraction exists elsewhere.\n- `finding`, seq **88**: KeePass masked residues plus KDBX3 verifier establish the exact master password; sensitive; interprets `j000114`, `j000115`.\n- `limitation`, seq **89**: preliminary hostkeys HMAC/layout testing found no match and neither validates nor refutes the deleted KeePass entry; sensitive; interprets `j000119`.\n- Unrecorded: `j000130`, `j000131`, `j000132`, `j000144`, `j000148`, `j000149`, `j000150`, DBX structural-header observation, and exact Q14 answer.\n\n## Board & Peers\n- `s42120106` owns Q3/Q4 and produced `j000105`/`j000107`; agent was asked in posts 134 and 153 for deleted entry provenance.\n- `s42120105` owns Q12/Q13 and needs the Q14